1. PHP Function for Secure Random String Generation, Hashing Password, and Session Management:

```php
<?php

function generateSecureRandomString($length = 32, $charset = '0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ') {
    if (!is_numeric($length) || strlen($length) > 2) {
        throw new Exception("Invalid length provided.");
    }

    $randomString = '';
    for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
        $index = random_int(0, strlen($charset) - 1);
        $randomString .= $charset[$index];
    }

    return $randomString;
}

function hashPassword($password, $algorithm = PASSWORD_BCRYPT, array $options = []) {
    if (!is_string($password) || strlen($password) < 8) {
        throw new Exception("Invalid password provided.");
    }

    return password_hash($password, $algorithm, $options);
}

function verifyPassword($hashedPassword, $password) {
    return password_verify($password, $hashedPassword);
}

session_start();

function setSessionToken($token) {
    $_SESSION['token'] = $token;
}

function getSessionToken() {
    if (isset($_SESSION['token'])) {
        return $_SESSION['token'];
    } else {
        return null;
    }
}

function removeSessionToken() {
    unset($_SESSION['token']);
}

?>
```

2. JavaScript Function for Reading a File Asynchronously using the fs library:

```javascript
const fs = require('fs');

function readFileSync(filePath) {
  if (!fs.existsSync(filePath)) {
    throw new Error(`The file ${filePath} does not exist.`);
  }

  const fileContents = fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf8');

  if (fileContents === null) {
    throw new Error('There was an error reading the file contents.');
  }

  return fileContents;
}
```

