The function finds the first occurrence of the `target` string in the forward list using `std::find_if()`. If the target is found, the function inserts the value after the target using `std::insert_after()`. If the target is not found, it appends the value to the end of the list.

Memory management is handled by using `emplace_back()` and exception handling is implemented with a try-catch block. The function returns true if the insertion was successful (i.e., the first string was found in the list), and false otherwise.

