3. Design a retry mechanism using Reactor's backpressure strategy:

```java
@Autowired
private WebClient webClient;

private Mono<WeatherData> fetchWeatherData(String location) {
    return webClient.get()
            .uri("http://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather?q=" + location + "&appid={API_KEY}")
            .retrieve()
            .onStatus(HttpStatus::is5xxServerError, signalType -> Mono.error(new ApiException("Server error")))
            .onStatus(httpStatus -> httpStatus.codeValue() >= 400 && httpStatus.codeValue() < 500, signalType -> Mono.error(new ApiException("Bad request or unauthorized")))
            .retryWhen(Retry.backoff(10, Duration.ofSeconds(2))
                    .doOnRetry(RetrySignal::retryIfThrowableTypeMatch)
                    .filter(RetrySignal::isRetryNeeded)
            )
            .bodyToMono(WeatherData.class);
}
